                <pb facs="0290" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.857 Athenia/1: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-outside-research" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-03">[undated]</date>.<lb/>[Received September 3, 1939—8:50
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Foreign Office has just telephoned that it is releasing to press report SS <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Athenia</hi> of Donaldson Line torpedoed 200 miles off
                    Malin Head with 1400 passengers aboard. S. O. S. received. Ship sinking
                    fast.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
